x</surname><given-names>L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Sale</surname><given-names>W.S.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Characterization of an axonemal type-1 phosphatase that regulates flagellar dynein activity</article-title><source>Mol. Biol. Cell.</source><volume>9</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>130a</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="Zhang1996"><citation citation-type="other">Zhang, D. 1996. Regulation of nitrate assimilation in <italic>Chlamydomonas reinhardtii</italic>. Ph.D. Thesis, University of Minnesota.</citation></ref><ref id="HZhangetal1994"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Herman</surname><given-names>P.L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Weeks</surname><given-names>D.P.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Gene isolation through genomic complementation using and indexed library of <italic>Chlamydomonas reinhardtii</italic> DNA</article-title><source>Plant Mol. Biol.</source><volume>24</volume><year>1994</year><fpage>663</fpage><lpage>672</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8155885</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn><p>used in this report: BAC, bacterial artificial chromosome&#x0003b; Dhc, dynein heavy chain&#x0003b; IC, intermediate chain&#x0003b; LC, light chain&#x0003b; OA, outer arm&#x0003b; P-loop, phosphate binding motif&#x0003b; P1-P4, Pn, Pc, P-loops 1-4, NH2- and COOH-terminal P-loop&#x0003b; RT-PCR, reverse transcriptase PCR</p></fn></fn-group></back><floats-wrap><table-wrap position="float" id="T1"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Strains Used in this Study</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr valign="bottom"><th align="left">Strain name</th><th align="center">Dynein defect</th><th align="center">Swimming phenotype</th><th align="center">Reference</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr valign="bottom" align="left"><td>Wild-type (137c)</td><td>None</td><td>Wild-type</td><td><xref ref-type="bib" rid="Harris1989">Harris 1989</xref></td></tr><tr valign="top" align="left"><td>pf9-2</td><td>I1 complex</td><td>Slow, smooth swimming</td><td><xref ref-type="bib" rid="Porteretal1992">Porter et al. 1992</xref></td></tr><tr valign="top" align="left"><td><italic>pf9-2 arg2</italic></td><td>I1 complex</td><td>Slow, smooth swimming</td><td><xref ref-type="bib" rid="Porteretal1992">Porter et al. 1992</xref></td></tr><tr valign="top" align="left"><td>pf28</td><td>Outer arm</td><td>Slow, jerky swimming</td><td><xref ref-type="bib" rid="MitchellandRosenbaum1985">Mitchell and Rosenbaum 1985</xref></td></tr><tr valign="top" align="left"><td>oda2</td><td>Outer arm</td><td>Slow, jerky swimming</td><td><xref ref-type="bib" rid="Kamiya1988">Kamiya 1988</xref></td></tr><tr valign="top" align="left"><td><italic>pf9-2 pf28 arg2</italic></td><td>Outer arm &#x00026; I1 complex</td><td>Short, paralyzed flagella</td><td>This study</td></tr><tr valign="top" align="left"><td>cW1 cotransformants</td><td/><td/><td/></tr><tr valign="top" align="left"><td>C1</td><td>Outer arm, partial I1</td><td>Slow, jerky swimming</td><td>This study</td></tr><tr valign="top" align="left"><td>E2</td><td>Outer arm, partial I1</td><td>Slow, jerky swimming</td><td>This study</td></tr><tr valign="top" align="left"><td>F2</td><td>Outer arm, partial I1</td><td>Slow, jerky swimming</td><td>This study</td></tr><tr valign="top" align="left"><td>F3</td><td>Outer arm, partial I1</td><td>Slow, jerky swimming</td><td>This study</td></tr><tr valign="top" align="left"><td>F4</td><td>Outer arm, partial I1</td><td>Slow, jerky swimming</td><td>This study</td></tr><tr valign="top" align="left"><td>F5</td><td>Outer arm, partial I1</td><td>Slow, jerky swimming</td><td>This study</td></tr><tr valign="top" align="left"><td>F7</td><td>Outer arm, partial I1</td><td>Slow, jerky swimming</td><td>This study</td></tr><tr valign="top" align="left"><td>G3</td><td>Outer arm, partial I1</td><td>Slow, j